    tip: "After the comma, ask: who did the *-ing*? The answer must be the subject that comes next. If it isn't, rewrite with *when, while, because* or *after* and a full clause.",
    note: "Participle clauses are much more common in writing than in conversation. In everyday American speech, people usually say *While I was walking home, I saw…* Use participle clauses in emails, essays and reports to sound concise.",
